  "goodToKnow": "Die Loyalität is loyalty: Loyalität gegenüber dem Arbeitgeber, Parteiloyalität. In German labour law, employees owe their employer a duty of loyalty (Loyalitätspflicht), which church employers interpret especially strictly. The native German word is die Treue, which appears in Treue um Treue and in the famously loyal dog breed reputation. Loyal means loyal. Pronounced lo-ya-li-TAIT. It has no plural."
